"""Build the final scientific report from verified analysis and saved solver histories."""
import csv,datetime,json,statistics
from pathlib import Path
R=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
s=json.loads((R/'data/analysis/summary.json').read_text());assert s['complete'] and s['completed_cases']==22
runtimes=[];storage=0
for group in ['canaries04','completed05','completed06','completed07']:
 root=R/'data'/group
 storage+=sum(p.stat().st_size for p in root.rglob('*') if p.is_file())
 for f in sorted(root.glob('*/solve/*_steps.csv')):
  with f.open() as h:
   q=csv.reader(h);next(q);next(q);rows=list(q)
  times=[datetime.datetime.fromisoformat(x[1].strip()) for x in rows]
  gaps=[(b-a).total_seconds() for a,b in zip(times,times[1:])];assert all(x>=0 for x in gaps)
  # Explicitly exclude long gaps between distinct recovery attempts. Shorter
  # clean-stop/upload/resume pauses remain included; lost work is not in history.
  runtimes.append(dict(case=f.parent.parent.name,retained_history_minutes=sum(x for x in gaps if x<1800)/60,excluded_recovery_gap_minutes=sum(x for x in gaps if x>=1800)/60,group=group))
assert len(runtimes)==22
stats=dict(cases=runtimes,mean_minutes=statistics.mean(x['retained_history_minutes'] for x in runtimes),median_minutes=statistics.median(x['retained_history_minutes'] for x in runtimes),scientific_export_bytes=storage,method='First-to-last recorded solver timestamps, excluding gaps >=30 minutes between recovery attempts. Includes shorter checkpoint pauses; omits provisioning, final upload, and work lost after last saved checkpoint. These are approximate retained-history runtimes, not billed VM times.')
(R/'data/analysis/runtime-storage.json').write_text(json.dumps(stats,indent=2)+'\n')
lines=['# Two-tree pilot: 22 retained cases completed','', 'All 20 baseline and two larger-domain cases reached 180 simulated seconds, with passing startup/completion checks and hash-verified final archives. Two fine-grid controls were cancelled; grid convergence is **not established**. No completed case was rerun from the beginning.','', '## What was simulated','', 'One tree per simulation, selected from two abstract species-inspired geometry families, approximately 18–26 m tall, with generic crown fuels and burning static cylindrical trunk/branch particles. Species-specific chemistry, bark layers, embers and grass are absent. Crowns use weighted representative particles rather than resolved leaves; woody particles do not form resolved solid airflow obstacles. Ignition is an imposed 0.4 × 0.4 m, 1500 °C heating patch for 20 seconds. These results do not validate real species fire behaviour.','', 'The baseline gas grid is 0.5 m in a 48 × 32 × 40 m domain (491,520 cells); expanded domains are 64 × 48 × 56 m. The original single-crown training domain had 49,152 cells. The larger-domain comparison does not establish that the baseline domain could not be reduced.','', '## Burning after the imposed source','', f"Integrated combustion heat varies from {min(c['energy_kj'] for c in s['cases'])/1000:.2f} to {max(c['energy_kj'] for c in s['cases'])/1000:.2f} MJ. Energy released after 20 s accounts for {min(c['energy_after_20s_kj']/c['energy_kj'] for c in s['cases'])*100:.1f}%–{max(c['energy_after_20s_kj']/c['energy_kj'] for c in s['cases'])*100:.1f}% of each case's total. At 180 s all cases retain small nonzero HRR, ranging {min(c['final_hrr_kw'] for c in s['cases']):.3f}–{max(c['final_hrr_kw'] for c in s['cases']):.3f} kW. This is not proof of exact extinction or long-term sustained burning.", '', 'HRR is simulated combustion heat release, not the heater power. Tracked wet-mass loss includes drying and pyrolysis; it must not be labelled pure combustion or tree destruction. No validated binary ignition criterion was applied.','', '## Domain sensitivity','']
for x in s['domain_comparisons']:
 m=x['metrics']['energy_kj'];lines.append(f"- {x['baseline']}: expanded-domain total combustion energy differs by {m['relative_difference']*100:.2f}%.")
lines+=['','Only two paired domain controls were run. Agreement of these integrated energies does not demonstrate convergence of local temperatures, heat fluxes, all geometries, or gas-grid resolution.','', '## Runtime and storage','', f"The 22 saved output histories average {stats['mean_minutes']:.1f} minutes (median {stats['median_minutes']:.1f}), including shorter checkpoint pauses and excluding long recovery gaps. This omits provisioning, final archive upload and computation lost to Spot eviction. The last baseline case required multiple attempts; restarting from verified saved state preserved its progress. Scientific exports occupy {storage/1e9:.3f} GB. Full operational archives and checkpoints are separately retained privately.", '', 'The original 32 single-crown training solves averaged 6.23 minutes for the same 180 s horizon. This is not a controlled hardware benchmark: current geometry, tenfold baseline gas-cell count, fuel representation and checkpoint overhead differ.','', '## Per-case results','', '| Case | Energy (MJ) | After 20 s (MJ) | Final HRR (kW) | Tracked wet-mass loss (%) |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
for c in s['cases']:lines.append(f"| {c['case']} | {c['energy_kj']/1000:.3f} | {c['energy_after_20s_kj']/1000:.3f} | {c['final_hrr_kw']:.3f} | {c['tracked_mass_loss_fraction']*100:.3f} |")
lines+=['','Evidence: `summary.json`, `runtime-storage.json`, and the per-case collection proofs in canaries04/completed05/completed06/completed07. No neural model was trained by this pilot.']
(R/'data/analysis/report.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n');print('Final report generated for22 cases')
